1: different 0.65; v10: different 0.99; v11: different', 'shared quantity: merge by key (D197); groups joined: none', 'jev: e1192: same_statement 0.82; e956: same_statement 0.69; ', 'jev: e1192: same_statement 0.85; e956: same_statement 0.67; ']\n944 1 4 [\"shared quantity: merge by key (D197); groups joined: ['g4']\", 'jev: e1495: same_statement 0.93; e1570: same_statement 0.90;', 'jev: e1876: different 0.71; e294: different 1.00; e976: diff', 'jev: e669: different 0.95; e1365: different 0.92; e1662: dif']\n1236 1 4 [\"shared quantity: merge by key (D197); groups joined: ['g4']\", 'jev: e2535: different 0.95; e119: same_statement 0.48; e412:', 'jev: e219: different 0.95; e2367: different 1.00; e216: diff', 'jev: e1153: different 1.00; e1155: different 1.00; e2717: di']\n1375 1 9 ['shared quantity: merge by key (D197); groups joined: none', 'shared quantity: merge by key (D197); groups joined: none', 'jev: e2478: same_statement 0.87; e2318: same_statement 0.90;', 'jev: e2390: same_statement 0.86; e2693: different 1.00; e674']\n1565 1 3 ['shared quantity: merge by key (D197); groups joined: none', 'shared quantity: merge by key (D197); groups joined: none', 'jev: e2217: different 1.00; e1564: different 1.00; e2520: di', 'jev: e1097: different 1.00; e2036: different 1.00; e2037: di']\n1824 1 8 ['shared quantity: merge by key (D197); groups joined: none', 'jev: e4756: same_statement 0.96; e3306: same_statement 0.97;', 'jev: e4095: same_statement 0.93; e3485: same_statement 0.86;', 'jev: e1878: different 0.91; e465: same_statement 0.53; e3838']\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"agent_message","text":"**NOT READY.** The full-window preflight is in place, and the scorer now rejects zero draws and the wrong sign on the known positive. But the scorer can still count a dry draw as paid, the July replay can buy a request it was meant to reuse, and three W pairs are too strong given the evidence Jev saw.\n\n## Round-14 fixes\n\n- **Scorer and completion.** It now requires draw IDs 1, 2 and 3, rejects a missing READS answer, and checks both direction and `together` for the known positive. I independently reran the no-draw refusal. The remaining gap is that `census-reuse-dry` writes a real `draw.json` with `draw: \"1\"` and `counted: true`. I checked that file. The scorer would accept it alongside paid draws 2 and 3, even though its other link answers were faked. Record whether the draw used paid or fake transport, and make the final scorer reject a dry draw. [Scorer](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/read_census.py:105) · [Draw record and dry entry point](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/window_test.py:213) · [Scorer checks](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/scorer-checks.log:1)\n- **July reuse.** I verified that all three July archives contain both expected hashes. The dry replay reused both and proposed `v9 reads v14` with `together`. However, `july_answers` accepts any number of rows, and the completion check compares reuse against whatever it loaded. A missing row can therefore fall through to the paid transport and still count. Validate both pinned hashes before sending anything, and refuse an unexpected seq-148 request before it reaches the budget transport. Exercise both refusal paths at $0. [July reuse code](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/window_test.py:196) · [Archive loader](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/window_test.py:234) · [Dry replay](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/census-reuse-dry.log:65)\n- **Preflight and budget.** Full-window preflight is complete. I traced the three refusals to two successions already present in the final store and a view that closed after the recorded merge. The ten skips are D197 shared-quantity records that the preflight lookup cannot identify, so §3 should correct its explanation of those skips. The chronological replay covers them. D700 supplies the $0.10 ceiling, and the store lock, launcher registration and sequential budget plan stand. Estimated settlements of $0.066 plus one $0.0084 live reservation fit under that ceiling. [Preflight output](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/preflight-window.log:16) · [Preflight lookup](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/preflight.py:170) · [Budget plan](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/DESIGN.md:124) · [D700](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10515)\n\n## Registered W pairs\n\nThe sole R is justified. I read the material shown for all 43 W pairs and would move these three to O before scoring:\n\n- **`206:v2` — supply commitments versus capacity backstops.** The shown evidence says NVIDIA agreed to repurchase unsold GPU capacity at a pre-agreed price. The supply-commitments question gives a $119B amount and ties it to hyperscaler order books, but leaves the scope of the reported commitments open. The repurchase obligation is a concrete reason to consider a link. The evidence leaves its inclusion uncertain. [Registered pair](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/expected-links.md:16) · [READS criterion](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/links.py:22)\n- **`746:v1` and `746:v2` — FY2027 gross margin versus FY2027 credit support.** Jev saw that supported capacity earns NVIDIA both product revenue and a share of cloud revenue, and that the guarantees can require NVIDIA to buy back unsold capacity. Those are specific revenue-mix and cost-exposure paths into gross margin. The material leaves their accounting and materiality uncertain, which makes O the defensible mark. [Registered margin pairs](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/expected-links.md:44) · [Evidence shown by the request builder](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/jev_matching.py:64)\n\nBefore sending, exclude dry draws from final scoring, make July reuse fail closed before any seq-148 purchase, and move the three pairs to O and rerun the $0 scoring checks.\n\n**NOT READY**"}}
